          "en": "-: In our little basic first application we're working on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.85,
          "end": 7.68,
          "en": "where we added a couple of components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.68,
          "end": 10.86,
          "en": "we covered a lot of key aspects of a basic Angular app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.86,
          "end": 13.14,
          "en": "How it starts and how to use components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.14,
          "end": 17.25,
          "en": "the base building block of any Angular app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.25,
          "end": 21.57,
          "en": "But thus far, we only output static content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.57,
          "end": 23.43,
          "en": "the server component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.43,
          "end": 25.26,
          "en": "That's not super interesting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.26,
          "end": 26.67,
          "en": "We did even more than that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.67,
          "end": 28.92,
          "en": "in the first section of this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.92,
          "end": 32.01,
          "en": "So let's change this to output some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.01,
          "end": 34.44,
          "en": "which is kind of dynamic at least,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.44,
          "end": 37.26,
          "en": "which is not hard coded into the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.26,
          "end": 39.06,
          "en": "Time for some data binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.06,
          "end": 40.62,
          "en": "What is data binding?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.62,
          "end": 42.99,
          "en": "You could basically translate data binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.99,
          "end": 45.3,
          "en": "with communication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 45.3,
          "end": 48.27,
          "en": "Communication between your TypeScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.27,
          "end": 51.75,
          "en": "of your component, your business logic, and the template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.75,
          "end": 53.43,
          "en": "so what the user sees,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 53.43,
          "end": 56.1,
          "en": "because you might have some result in your TypeScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 56.1,
          "end": 58.38,
          "en": "because you fetched something from a server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 58.38,
          "end": 60.36,
          "en": "or finished some calculation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 60.36,
          "end": 62.31,
          "en": "which you want to display to the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 62.31,
          "end": 65.13,
          "en": "and the only thing the user sees is the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 65.13,
          "end": 67.08,
          "en": "So we need some kind of communication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 67.08,
          "end": 70.41,
          "en": "between both pieces to be able to really well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 70.41,
          "end": 72.15,
          "en": "do something in our app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 72.15,
          "end": 73.98,
          "en": "That is where data binding comes into play",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 73.98,
          "end": 76.92,
          "en": "because it is responsible for this communication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 76.92,
          "end": 79.26,
          "en": "We get different ways of communication now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 79.26,
          "end": 82.05,
          "en": "For example, we want to output data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 82.05,
          "end": 86.55,
          "en": "from our TypeScript code in the HTML code in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 86.55,
          "end": 88.95,
          "en": "We can use string interpolation for this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 88.95,
          "end": 91.05,
          "en": "You saw this in the first section of the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 91.05,
          "end": 93.36,
          "en": "It's the syntax with the double curly braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 93.36,
          "end": 96.9,
          "en": "and then some property name or some expression in between,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 96.9,
          "end": 98.88,
          "en": "or property binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 98.88,
          "end": 99.87,
          "en": "We will have a closer look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 99.87,
          "end": 102.12,
          "en": "at all of these forms of course in the next lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 102.12,
          "end": 104.72999999999999,
          "en": "so we will learn what this then is and how it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 104.72999999999999,
          "end": 107.85,
          "en": "The syntax basically uses these strange square brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 107.85,
          "end": 112.53,
          "en": "around HTML attributes, but again, I will come back to this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 112.53,
          "end": 116.49000000000001,
          "en": "Sometimes though, the other direction is interesting too.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 116.49000000000001,
          "end": 118.35,
          "en": "If the user clicks a button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 118.35,
          "end": 119.91,
          "en": "you can kind of think of the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 119.91,
          "end": 121.74,
          "en": "clicking this button on the template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 121.74,
          "end": 123.57,
          "en": "because again, the template is the thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 123.57,
          "end": 125.19,
          "en": "with which the user interacts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 125.19,
          "end": 128.55,
          "en": "which he sees and where he is also able to click buttons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 128.55,
          "end": 130.26,
          "en": "So if we click a button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 130.26,
          "end": 133.2,
          "en": "we maybe want to trigger something in our TypeScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 133.2,
          "end": 135.3,
          "en": "So now we need the other direction,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 135.3,
          "end": 137.49,
          "en": "and we can get this other direction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 137.49,
          "end": 140.91,
          "en": "We can react to user events with event binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 140.91,
          "end": 142.86,
          "en": "so we can bind to, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 142.86,
          "end": 146.73,
          "en": "a click event to execute some code whenever it occurs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 146.73,
          "end": 150.63,
          "en": "And we also have one additional form of data binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 150.63,
          "end": 153.09,
          "en": "where we combine both directions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 153.09,
          "end": 157.14,
          "en": "Two-way data binding, where we are able to react events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 157.14,
          "end": 159.84,
          "en": "and output something at the same time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 159.84,
          "end": 161.88,
          "en": "Might not be super clear how this works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 161.88,
          "end": 164.43,
          "en": "but that's why we will now have a detailed look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 164.43,
          "end": 167.523,
          "en": "at all four forms in the next lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
